# mcp_pdf

Contract for the opt-in PDF tool server (`luxe-pdf-mcp`). This package is a
CAPABILITY MODULE: it is reachable only from `luxe chat` / `luxe code` when
the user attaches it (`--mcp pdf`), and it is invisible to the
benchmark/maintain path.

The module exists for one recurring real-world job: a PDF that a viewer
refuses to let you print, edit, or fill even though you are entitled to do
so — the owner-password/permission-flag restriction that government and
institutional forms ship with. `pdf_unlock` clears it with `qpdf --decrypt`
and then makes the form actually fillable (NeedAppearances + dropped usage
rights). Everything else in the module is the surrounding workflow:
inspect, extract, fill, overlay, convert, print.

## Must
- Keep `ops.py` free of MCP imports: every operation is a plain function
  taking and returning JSON-safe values, so `tests/test_mcp_pdf.py` can
  exercise the whole surface with no server running
- Take explicit input/output paths on every operation. When `output` is
  omitted, derive a SIBLING of the input named `<stem>-<op><suffix>`
- Never write over the input path. `_resolve_out` raises when the resolved
  output equals the input, and refuses an existing output unless the caller
  passes `overwrite=True`
- Raise `PdfToolError` with a remedy in the text — what to install
  (`brew install qpdf poppler`), what to sync (`uv sync --extra pdf`), or
  what to toggle (`/write`) — matching luxe's self-explaining-failure
  convention. A bare `FileNotFoundError` from a missing CLI is a bug
- Fail honestly on a user (open) password we were not given: say the file
  needs the password and stop. Never attempt recovery of an unknown password
- Refuse to print to a label printer (name matching `*QL*` / `*label*`)
  unless the caller passes `allow_label=True`; the default target is a
  document printer
- Declare mutating tools in the server's `gate_tools` so `luxe chat`
  withholds them until `/write`: everything that writes a file or spools a
  job. `pdf_info` / `pdf_text` / `pdf_form_fields` / `pdf_printers` are
  read-only and always available

## Must not
- Add anything here to `luxe.tools.TOOL_FNS`, `run_single`'s default tool
  list, or any benchmark config — a reproducible benchmark must not grow a
  dependency on local PDF binaries or a printer
- Enable the server by default. `configs/mcp.yaml` `client.servers` stays
  `[]`; the repo ships a COMMENTED example stanza only
- Make `pypdf` / `reportlab` / `pillow` base dependencies. They live in the
  `[pdf]` optional extra; importing this package without them must produce
  the install remedy, not a traceback at import time
- Shell out through a shell string. Every subprocess call is an argv list
  with `shell=False`
- Crack, brute-force, or work around a user (open) password

## Owns
- src/luxe/mcp_pdf/**
- tests/test_mcp_pdf.py

## Forbids
- src/luxe/mcp_pdf/**/prompts.py
